From: CARGT <engineering@cargt.com>
Subject: [PATCH] init-resize: skip growing bootfs/vendorfs/rootfs, they're
 fixed-size A/B slots now

bootfs, vendorfs and rootfs are duplicated into -a/-b RAUC OTA slots,
each built to (and flashed at) a fixed size with no "remaining space"
to grow into - unlike userfs, which is intentionally built small and
grown once to fill whatever's left on the eMMC.

This script matches partitions by ext4 filesystem label with a plain
prefix (root*/vendor*/boot*), and both the -a and -b slot of a given
filesystem get built with the same label - so under the old single-
bank naming this ran once per filesystem, but now runs (and does a
full e2fsck -c bad-blocks scan) against *both* A and B slots, on the
first boot of whichever slot happens to be newly installed. For RAUC,
"newly installed" means every OTA update's first boot into the slot
that was just updated - not just a one-time factory cost. Since these
partitions never need growing, drop the fsck+resize2fs work for them
entirely and just log that they were seen.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not sent upstream to ST - specific to a
custom A/B partition scheme]

--- a/init-resize.sh
+++ b/init-resize.sh
@@ -58,16 +58,13 @@
                                     /sbin/resize2fs $DEVICE
                                     ;;
                                 root*)
-                                    echo "RESIZE ROOTFS [$DEVICE]"
-                                    /sbin/e2fsck -f -y -c -C 0 $DEVICE && /sbin/resize2fs $DEVICE
+                                    echo "SKIP ROOTFS [$DEVICE] (fixed-size A/B slot)"
                                     ;;
                                 vendor*)
-                                    echo "RESIZE VENDORFS [$DEVICE]"
-                                    /sbin/e2fsck -f -y -c -C 0 $DEVICE && /sbin/resize2fs $DEVICE
+                                    echo "SKIP VENDORFS [$DEVICE] (fixed-size A/B slot)"
                                     ;;
                                 boot*)
-                                    echo "RESIZE BOOTFS [$DEVICE]"
-                                    /sbin/e2fsck -f -y -c -C 0 $DEVICE && /sbin/resize2fs $DEVICE
+                                    echo "SKIP BOOTFS [$DEVICE] (fixed-size A/B slot)"
                                     ;;
                                 *)
                                     ;;
